ra  factors will periodically issue updates  to their recommended procedures so this  is allows you to keep all the documents  for each one and show for a particular  test which version of the SOP was  followed for that test equipment all of  your equipment needs to be maintained it  needs to be periodically tested and  calibrated here we have the dates of the  last calibration we have the schedule  for the next calibration the limbs will  automatically give you a reminder when  the next calibration is due or the next  maintenance is due so all of your  maintenance and calibration is done as  per the manufacturer guidelines  measurements traceability each one of  your tests which are the live test  results that you're going to be giving  to your clients need to be able to be  traced back to the last calibration and  control study that was done to show that  your results are accurate this allows  for comparability of the test and  calibration results here you can see we  can take any particular tasks and trace  it back to the calibration that was done  on the same instrument using the same  SOP and the same reagents so that we  know that we're getting accurate test  results this is also very useful in your  defense ability so if any testing result  is a question you can show but we did  the same test using the same calibration  on the same instrument with the same  control and based on the control we are  getting the correct results the  reporting of results after you've  executed and decided to release  generally by the laboratory manager the  results you want to make it available to  the client so here we can see within the  limbs the test results in a format that  would be viewed by the laboratory  director we  then view the laboratory results and  decide to release them when they're  released the client it's usually done in  the form of a certificate of analysis so  this certificate of analysis is in a  format that's readable to the customer  the grower or the ed